## Project Number/Title 

* Authors: Alexander Lynch, Samuel Siew
* Group name: Group-98

## Overview

The program implements parallel merge sort in C using threads. It sorts a randomly generated array of integers by recursively splitting the array into two and creating a new thread for each half. The number of levels created is determined by the user input, as well as the number of elements to be sorted and the seed to be used for the random number generator. 

